    <briefdescription>
<para>Guard that detects use-after-move in debug builds. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>In production, this is a no-op. In debug mode, it detects invalid access.</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">T<sp/>obj<sp/>=<sp/>create();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="classthemis_1_1safety_1_1_move_guard_1a1828f42599f59d9156838604f341a2fc" kindref="member">MoveGuard&lt;T&gt;</ref><sp/>guard(obj);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>container<sp/>=<sp/>std::move(obj);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Guard<sp/>destructor<sp/>verifies<sp/>obj<sp/>not<sp/>used<sp/>after<sp/>move</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>obj.foo();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>This<sp/>would<sp/>be<sp/>flagged<sp/>(or<sp/>UB)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
